{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Whatsoever hath not, etc.</b> What does Scripture say? For I might say: it is permitted only if it raises its signs onto dry land — from where do I know [it is permitted] if it left them in the water? Scripture says: ״כֹּל אֲשֶׁר אֵין לוֹ סְנַפִּיר וְקַשְׂקֶשֶׂת בַּמַּיִם״ — this teaches: if it had them in the water, even though it left them upon its emergence, it is permitted (Sifra)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:48.094899897Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}